### MongoDB Express REST API - REST Client requests
### Start the server with: npm start
### Replace the itemId value after the POST request with the returned MongoDB _id.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@itemId = REPLACE_WITH_MONGODB_OBJECT_ID

### 1. Get all items
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/items

### 2. Create an item (copy its returned _id into @itemId above)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Study for operating systems",
  "description": "Review synchronization and deadlocks",
  "completed": false
}

### 3. Get one item
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/items/{{itemId}}

### 4. Update one or more fields
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/items/{{itemId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "completed": true
}

### 5. Delete the item
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/items/{{itemId}}

### 6. Confirm a deleted/nonexistent item returns 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/items/000000000000000000000000

### 7. Invalid ID returns 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/items/not-an-object-id
